```spl
`SOC Lab Detection Rule`
`Rule Name: Security Group Membership Tampering / Privilege Escalation`
`Event IDs: 4728 (Member added to global security group), 4732 (Member added to local security group), 4756 (Member added to universal security group)`
`MITRE ATT&CK: T1098 (Account Manipulation), T1078 (Valid Accounts)`
`Severity: High (When added to Administrators or Remote Desktop Users)`
`Data Source: WinEventLog:Security | index=blue`
`Description: Detects when accounts are elevated into privileged groups such as local Administrators or privileged domain groups.`
```

index=blue (EventCode=4728 OR EventCode=4732 OR EventCode=4756)
| eval Target_Group=coalesce(TargetUserName,Target_Group_Name)
| eval Added_Member=coalesce(MemberName,Member_Name)
| eval Admin_Actor=coalesce(SubjectUserName,Subject_Account_Name,user)
| eval Group_Type=case(
    EventCode=4728,"Global Group",
    EventCode=4732,"Local Security Group",
    EventCode=4756,"Universal Group",
    true(),"Other")
| table _time host Admin_Actor Added_Member Target_Group Group_Type EventCode Message
| sort - _time
